From c2481c1c20ebd2d87255fa14db932c7c120f3649 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:19:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] render: hold the shared atlas's dynamic rows in bands
 as they are written

The atlas's dynamic part (map, skin, trim, world-icon and pack-icon
slots, the on-screen keyboard's text, the animated sprites, the glyph
rows) was a full RGBA texture: 46 MiB of GPU memory on the default
resources, nearly all of it slots a session never fills.

Hold it in bands of 64 rows, only the ones written to. A band is held
from the first write into it, as the next band of a texture that grows
by it (the bands held so far copied over on the GPU). A page table in a
uniform (the atlas's rows, the band size, each band's place) tells the
shaders where each band is; a band never written reads as transparent
black, as the empty slot did. atlas_size reads the atlas's height from
it. The initial upload holds only the bands with something in them.

The HUD bind group gains binding 6 and the entity one binding 9 (the
table); both are remade before the frame's first pass when the texture
grew. The whole-atlas copy places each held band where it belongs.

Default resources: 1 band (1 MiB) at the title, 4 in a world with a map
in hand and unifont chat, against 46 MiB before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
